cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Dual Neprilysin / DPP-IV Inhibitor Discovery Pipeline:
  a reproducible structure-based virtual screening workflow
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to this pipeline, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohammed Mujtaba Shahnawaz
    family-names: Khan
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # <- add yours
repository-code: 'https://github.com/<YOUR-USERNAME>/nep-dpp4-dual-inhibitor-screen'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible structure-based virtual screening pipeline for the
  identification of molecules with dual inhibitory activity against
  neprilysin and dipeptidyl peptidase-IV, developed as a candidate
  therapeutic strategy for type 2 diabetes in patients at risk of heart
  failure with reduced ejection fraction. The workflow covers target
  preparation and docking validation, database mining and library
  construction, a docking and rescoring cascade, cross-target selection
  for dual activity, and constrained scaffold enumeration with
  antitarget counter-screening. This repository is a documented
  reimplementation of an undergraduate research project.
keywords:
  - virtual screening
  - molecular docking
  - neprilysin
  - DPP-IV
  - dual inhibitor
  - computer-aided drug design
  - type 2 diabetes
  - heart failure
